[acct2-ocr] SDK 0074, 2026-11-12 (the owner, 17:02: "The game window will briefly open on another screen if the
mouse is focused there. The window will then switch to the other screen. Our display binding logic is flawed.").
What it does: WindowSDL::OpenImpl makes the window centered on the chosen display (0068's monitor_name / monitor)
instead of making it with no position and moving it there with SDL_SetWindowPosition before it is shown.
Why: SDL gives a window made without a position no position hint (X11: no USPosition in WM_NORMAL_HINTS), so when it
is first shown the window manager places it where new windows go, on the screen the mouse is on, and SDL moves it to
the chosen screen a moment later. Measured on the owner's PC (X11, two screens, the mouse on screen 1, screen 2
chosen; a 480x270 test window with the SDK's own SDL 3.5.0, never focused): the old way was first viewable on screen
1 at 25 ms and on screen 2 at 32 ms; the new way was first viewable on screen 2 and stayed there. Fullscreen resolves
against the display the window is on, so it now goes fullscreen on the chosen screen from the start too.
Unchanged: the automatic choice (no position, the system decides), Wayland (the compositor places windows),
Window::SetDisplayChoice / ApplyNewDisplayChoice (moving an open window when F2's Display row changes), Windows and
macOS (where a hidden window's position was already used as it is shown).

